# Build context exclusions for `docker build` / `docker compose build`.
#
# Without this file the entire worktree is tarred and sent to the daemon —
# including target/ (gigabytes of cargo output) and .git/. That makes the
# first `docker compose -f docker-compose.local.yml build` painfully slow
# and gives BuildKit no cache benefit on iteration.
#
# Pattern syntax matches .gitignore.

# Rust build artifacts — biggest single win.
target/
**/target/

# Git internals — never needed at build time.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Editor / tooling state
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# CI / docs — the Dockerfile only needs Cargo manifests + source.
.github/
docs/
*.md

# Other compose files — they're not part of the build, but leaving them in
# the context busts the cache whenever you tweak one.
docker-compose*.yml
.env*

# Keycloak realm import is mounted at runtime, not baked into the image.
keycloak/
